Hello -

I was playing happily on a Nokia phone, getting ready for the ascension
run. Was -49 AC, found heaps of magic markers, bone files, everything was
perfect.

Then the phone decided to be evil and reset itself. Of course, the version
of Nethack that was compiled for Symbian lacked the recover program :-(

... so I copied the character_99.* files to my computer (Linux) and ran
recover, which resulted in character.sav

The Nokia nethack would not load character.sav, complaining about a wrong
version. Some hexediting with the .sav files made me notice that 0x00 to
0x10 in the new .sav file was blank, i.e. all 0x0. So I copied the first
0x10 bytes from the other save files (they were all the same) to the new
.sav file.

Now the file starts to load, but then stops with "saved game was not
yours". According to what I found online, the problem lies with restore.c,
which makes nethack refuse to upload a save file if the UID included in
the file is not the same as the UID running the program.

Symbian on Nokia is not multisystem... so my question is: does anyone know
more or less where are the byte(s) which set the UID? I could look for
them in the properly saved files, and replace them in the incorrect file...

I will keep trying, but if anyone knows, it would save me some time... :-)

